**Bug:** on the Achievements page, the four ladder badges in the "Ascent" section show in English in every app language: *Getting Going*, *Halfway Up*, *Seasoned*, *Top of the Ladder*. Ankita reported this today.

**Cause:** migration `1950200000000-SeedXpLevelBadges` inserted them with raw SQL. That skips `createBadge`, which is where a badge gets translated, so their `translations` column is `null` and the app falls back to English.

**Why the existing backfill wasn't safe:** `POST /api/v1/badges/make-translations` re-translated **every** badge into **every** language and replaced the whole `translations` object. That would overwrite any badge translation someone had corrected by hand.

**Change:** it now requests only the languages a badge is missing and merges them into what's already there. A language counts as missing when:
- it has no entry or no name;
- it has no description while the badge has one;
- its name is identical to the English one. `translateObjectToLanguages` stores the English source as the "translation" when a call fails, so an English copy means an earlier failure.

**After release:** run `POST /api/v1/badges/make-translations` once as an admin. Only the four ladder badges, plus any other badge with gaps, get translated.

**Checked:**
- `jest src/badge`: 85 tests pass, 4 of them new:
  - a seeded badge gets all four languages;
  - a fully translated badge is left untouched;
  - a partly translated badge gets only the gap, with the rest kept;
  - an English copy is re-translated.
- `eslint` and `tsc` pass.

